<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh 1996 inflation slows to 28.7 pct.</title>
<headline>Kazakh 1996 inflation slows to 28.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kazakhstan's inflation slowed to 28.7 percent last year from 60.3 percent in 1995, the State Statistics Committee said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>    KAZAKH CPI INFLATION	Dec 96    Nov 96     Dec 95</p>
<p>    mth/mth pct change	   +0.8	+2.4	 +3.6</p>
<p>    yr/yr pct change	    +28.7     +27.7	+60.3</p>
<p>The National Bank is forecasting inflation of 17-18 percent this year.</p>
<p>--Dmitry Solovyov, Almaty Newsroom, + 7 3272 509410</p>
</text>
